#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:9
msgid "Use Markdown Architectural Decision Records"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:11
msgid "Context and Problem Statement"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:13
msgid ""
"pyvista-wasm is accumulating architecturally significant decisions — e.g."
" the choice of vtk-wasm as the C++ VTK binding layer, the TypeScript glue"
" architecture that bridges vtk-wasm bindings to the Python-facing PyVista"
" API, and the WebAssembly runtime strategy for running PyVista entirely "
"in the browser. Today these decisions live only in issue threads and PR "
"descriptions, which makes the rationale hard to find later and easy to "
"lose. We want to record architectural decisions made in this project — "
"whether they concern the architecture, the code, or other fields — in a "
"consistent, version-controllable way. Which format and structure should "
"these records follow?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:15
msgid "Decision Drivers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:17
msgid ""
"**Explicit rationale**: Implicit assumptions should be made explicit so "
"future contributors can understand *why* a decision was made, not just "
"*what* was decided. See also [\"A rational design process: How and why to"
" fake it\"](https://doi.org/10.1109/TSE.1986.6312940)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:18
msgid ""
"**Version control friendliness**: Records must be plain text that diffs "
"and reviews well in Git alongside the code they govern."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:19
msgid ""
"**Low overhead**: pyvista-wasm is a small project; the format must be "
"lean enough that writing a record does not feel like a burden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:20
msgid ""
"**Comprehensibility**: The structure should be easy to read and scan for "
"both authors and reviewers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:21
msgid ""
"**Tooling availability**: Prefer a format with active maintenance and "
"supporting tooling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:22
msgid ""
"**Generality**: The format should capture any decision — architectural, "
"design, or tooling — not only a narrow class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:24
msgid "Considered Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:26
msgid ""
"[MADR](https://adr.github.io/madr/) 4.0.0 — The Markdown Architectural "
"Decision Records"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:27
msgid ""
"[Michael Nygard's template](http://thinkrelevance.com/blog/2011/11/15"
"/documenting-architecture-decisions) — The first incarnation of the term "
"\"ADR\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:28
msgid ""
"[Sustainable Architectural Decisions](https://www.infoq.com/articles"
"/sustainable-architectural-design-decisions) — The Y-Statements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:29
msgid ""
"Other templates listed at "
"[https://github.com/joelparkerhenderson/architecture_decision_record](https://github.com/joelparkerhenderson/architecture_decision_record)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:30
#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:94
msgid "Formless — No conventions for file format and structure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:32
msgid "Decision Outcome"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:34
msgid ""
"Chosen option: \"MADR 4.0.0\", because it best fits the decision drivers."
" It is a lean Markdown template with optional sections, captures any "
"decision (not only pure architecture), and is actively maintained with "
"tooling support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:36
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:38
msgid ""
"Good, because architectural rationale will live alongside the code in "
"`docs/decisions/` and travel through the same review/PR flow."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:39
msgid ""
"Good, because the consistent `NNNN-title-with-dashes.md` filename "
"convention makes records discoverable and sortable."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:40
msgid ""
"Good, because the MADR template's optional sections (Decision Drivers, "
"Pros and Cons of the Options, Confirmation, More Information) keep short "
"decisions short while scaling to complex ones."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:41
msgid ""
"Good, because YAML front matter (`status`, `date`, `decision-makers`, "
"`consulted`, `informed`) gives lightweight metadata for tracking decision"
" lifecycle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:42
msgid ""
"Bad, because contributors must learn the template and remember to open a "
"record for significant decisions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:43
msgid ""
"Neutral, because we adopt the MADR conventions as-is rather than forking "
"the template, trading a little flexibility for staying on a maintained "
"upstream."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:45
msgid "Confirmation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:47
msgid "Compliance with this decision will be confirmed by:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:49
msgid ""
"A `docs/decisions/` directory exists in the repository containing the "
"MADR template (`adr-template.md`) copied from the [MADR 4.0.0 "
"release](https://github.com/adr/madr/tree/4.0.0/template)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:50
msgid ""
"The first concrete record, `docs/decisions/0000-use-markdown-"
"architectural-decision-records.md`, mirrors this issue's content and is "
"merged via PR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:51
msgid ""
"Subsequent architecturally significant proposals (e.g. the TypeScript "
"glue layer design for bridging vtk-wasm bindings to the PyVista API) are "
"accompanied by a MADR record linked from the issue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:52
msgid ""
"A CI step (e.g. markdownlint with MADR's `.markdownlint` config) lints "
"records on PRs touching `docs/decisions/`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:54
msgid "Pros and Cons of the Options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:56
msgid "MADR 4.0.0 — The Markdown Architectural Decision Records"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:58
msgid "See [https://adr.github.io/madr/](https://adr.github.io/madr/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:60
msgid ""
"Good, because it is plain Markdown, satisfying the version-control-"
"friendliness and low-overhead drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:61
msgid ""
"Good, because the structure (Context and Problem Statement → Decision "
"Drivers → Considered Options → Decision Outcome → Pros and Cons of the "
"Options → More Information) is comprehensible and scales from one-"
"paragraph to multi-page decisions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:62
msgid ""
"Good, because the project is vivid: 4.0.0 released 2024-09-17, with "
"examples, a changelog, and tooling (markdownlint config, init scripts)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:63
msgid ""
"Good, because it captures *any* decision, satisfying the generality "
"driver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:64
msgid ""
"Neutral, because it ships optional YAML front matter that we will adopt "
"but is not strictly required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:65
msgid ""
"Bad, because it introduces a small documentation convention contributors "
"must learn."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:67
msgid "Michael Nygard's template"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:69
msgid ""
"See [http://thinkrelevance.com/blog/2011/11/15/documenting-architecture-"
"decisions](http://thinkrelevance.com/blog/2011/11/15/documenting-"
"architecture-decisions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:71
msgid "Good, because it is the original ADR template and is widely cited."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:72
msgid ""
"Good, because it is minimal: Title, Context, Decision, Status, "
"Consequences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:73
msgid ""
"Neutral, because its brevity is appealing but leaves no room for "
"comparing options or capturing drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:74
msgid ""
"Bad, because it lacks a \"Considered Options\" / \"Pros and Cons\" "
"section, so alternatives and their trade-offs are not recorded."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:75
msgid ""
"Bad, because there is no maintained tooling or canonical Markdown source;"
" many variants exist."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:77
msgid "Sustainable Architectural Decisions — The Y-Statements"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:79
msgid ""
"See [https://www.infoq.com/articles/sustainable-architectural-design-"
"decisions](https://www.infoq.com/articles/sustainable-architectural-"
"design-decisions)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:81
msgid ""
"Good, because the Y-Statement (In the context of `Z`, facing `Q`, we "
"decided `S` to achieve `B`, accepting `D`) is concise and forces explicit"
" trade-offs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:82
msgid ""
"Neutral, because the format is more of a single-sentence pattern than a "
"full document template."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:83
msgid ""
"Bad, because it does not scale to multi-option comparisons with detailed "
"pros and cons."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:84
msgid "Bad, because it is less widely adopted and has less tooling than MADR."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:86
msgid "Other templates listed at joelparkerhenderson/architecture_decision_record"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:88
msgid ""
"See "
"[https://github.com/joelparkerhenderson/architecture_decision_record](https://github.com/joelparkerhenderson/architecture_decision_record)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:90
msgid ""
"Good, because the list offers many variants (Planguage, MADR, Nygard, "
"Y-Statement, etc.) so we could pick a niche fit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:91
msgid ""
"Neutral, because choosing one of the lesser-known templates would mean "
"self-maintaining it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:92
msgid ""
"Bad, because the variety itself is a cost: contributors would need to "
"learn whichever one we pick with less community documentation behind it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:96
msgid "Good, because there is zero upfront cost and no template to learn."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:97
msgid ""
"Bad, because records drift in style, omit rationale, and become hard to "
"find — failing the explicit-rationale and comprehensibility drivers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:98
msgid ""
"Bad, because without a `docs/decisions/` convention and filename pattern,"
" decisions stay scattered across issues and PRs, which is the situation "
"we are trying to escape."
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:100
msgid "More Information"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:102
msgid "MADR homepage: [https://adr.github.io/madr/](https://adr.github.io/madr/)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:103
msgid ""
"MADR 4.0.0 release: "
"[https://github.com/adr/madr/releases/tag/4.0.0](https://github.com/adr/madr/releases/tag/4.0.0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:104
msgid ""
"MADR template (development): "
"[https://github.com/adr/madr/blob/develop/template/adr-"
"template.md](https://github.com/adr/madr/blob/develop/template/adr-"
"template.md)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:105
msgid ""
"Initialization snippet: `npm install madr && mkdir -p docs/decisions && "
"cp node_modules/madr/template/* docs/decisions/`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../decisions/0000-use-markdown-architectural-decision-records.md:106
msgid ""
"This record, once accepted, will live at `docs/decisions/0000-use-"
"markdown-architectural-decision-records.md` mirroring MADR's own "
"ADR-0000."
msgstr ""

